--  A server whose state can be saved (ADR 0032, section 10, #881). State
--  is the server's state as a stream, starting with a format version
--  (Rose.Replacement writes and reads it), which another instance of the
--  program can start from, as its Saved argument. It changes nothing, and
--  carries no caps: a cap named in the state is given to the new instance
--  as the command's argument of that name. The reader is the caller's to
--  release when it is done with it.

interface Saveable is

   function State
     return interface Releasable_Reader;

end Saveable;
